<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amadeus V, Count of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1249–<a href="/years/1323">1323</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Amadeus the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amadeus V, called the Great, was Count of Savoy from 1285 until his death in 1323. He extended Savoyard rule, gaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bresse">Bresse</a> through his marriage to Sibylle of Baugé, and in 1294 settled his nephew Philip with the family's lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, the origin of the Savoy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> line. He was active in imperial and French politics and strengthened the county's position on both sides of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Amadeus V, Count of Savoy" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknow person · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_Amedeo_V_di_Savoia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
